<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Reuss</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Reuss was a German noble family descended from the medieval Vögte of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weida">Weida</a>, Gera and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plauen">Plauen</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, in which every male member was named Heinrich. Divided into an Elder and a Younger Line, it ruled several small counties and principalities, repeatedly partitioned, until the monarchy ended in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss.jpg" alt="House of Reuss" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Reuss-Lobenstein.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
